Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: qcom: cpr4pd: use the APC supply for arrays at the APM threshold

The MSM8953 Array Power Mux feeds the CPU memory arrays either from
VDD_MX or from the APC rail itself. cpr_vreg_set_voltage() parks the
rail at the APM threshold (850 mV), switches the mux and then moves to
the target, selecting the APC supply only when the target is strictly
above the threshold.

Downstream (cpr3-regulator.c, cpr3_regulator_switch_apm_mode()) selects
the high (APC) supply when new_volt >= apm_threshold_volt, and in
closed-loop mode pins any corner whose open-loop voltage is within the
APM hysteresis of the threshold to a floor of exactly the threshold, so
on stock such a corner always runs with the arrays on APC.

On this unit (speed bin 6, fusing revision 3) the 1804.8 MHz OPP
interpolates to 848 mV, rounded up to 850 mV, i.e. exactly the
threshold. Mainline therefore ran the top OPP with the arrays on MX,
while stock runs the same corner at 850 mV (measured: pm8953_s5 =
850000 uV at 1804.8 MHz) with the arrays on APC.

Use >= so the mux setting at the threshold matches the vendor driver.
Targets below or above the threshold are unaffected.
---
diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr4pd.c b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr4pd.c
index bcdd57bbe..2fbdb2643 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr4pd.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr4pd.c
@@ -242,7 +242,13 @@ static int cpr_vreg_set_voltage(struct cpr_drv *drv, u32 uv)
 
 		drv->uv = apm_thr_uv;
 
-		ret = cpr_apm_switch_supply(drv, uv > apm_thr_uv);
+		/*
+		 * Arrays go to the APC rail at and above the threshold, as
+		 * downstream does (new_volt >= apm_threshold_volt selects the
+		 * high supply). A target of exactly the threshold therefore
+		 * runs on APCC, not on MX.
+		 */
+		ret = cpr_apm_switch_supply(drv, uv >= apm_thr_uv);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
 	}
